  "title": "The Difference Between a Digitized Well Log and a Usable One",
  "summary": "Operators digitized their well logs years ago, but a scan only preserves the image of a document, not the depth tracks, curve scales, and spatial relationships that make the subsurface record usable as data. This piece shows why the hardest records to extract are also the most valuable, and how Pulse's vision-language models finally read well logs, schematics, and maps as structured, traceable data across even the faded and handwritten archive. | Pulse AI",
